invariant: INV-17
file: sha3_hw.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh keccak
reason: permute_blocks writes lane 7 to a stack slot of its own each
  round, as a compiler does that needs a 33rd register where arm64 has
  32. No wipe clears that slot, and every digest is still right.
  bin/sha3_hw_equiv_test copies the stack below each kind of call and
  finds the lane there, and the script builds it with clang for arm64,
  the one object that holds sha3_hw.c. The lane skips without docker,
  and this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
        for (int round = 0; round < 24; round++) {
--- new
        for (int round = 0; round < 24; round++) {
            volatile uint64_t kept_on_the_stack = vgetq_lane_u64(a7, 0);
            (void)kept_on_the_stack;
